WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.725
Here's the grammar — one picture that explains the whole notation.

2
00:00:03.725 --> 00:00:07.987
It revolves around Domain Events — something that happened in the business.

3
00:00:07.987 --> 00:00:09.625
Orange, past tense.

4
00:00:09.625 --> 00:00:12.537
An Actor issues a Command — an intention.

5
00:00:12.537 --> 00:00:13.900
Blue, imperative.

6
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:18.887
The Command lands on an Aggregate, which guards the rules and generates the event.

7
00:00:18.887 --> 00:00:23.825
…or on an external system we don't control — it still produces events.

8
00:00:23.825 --> 00:00:28.525
Events build Read Models — the information people read, shown on screen.

9
00:00:28.525 --> 00:00:32.750
Events also trigger Policies: whenever this happens, do that.

10
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:36.662
And a Policy invokes a new Command — the loop closes.

11
00:00:36.662 --> 00:00:43.850
Read it as a sentence: when a Ticket is Purchased, the Loyalty policy tells the system to Award Points.

